      "message": "**Issue #1 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: Hardcoded `snmp1` URI suffix is a brittle assumption\n\n**Issue**: After `Delete All SNMP Managers` empties the subscription list, the test attempts to delete `/redfish/v1/EventService/Subscriptions/snmp1`. The assumption is that `snmp1` will never exist after a full deletion. This is generally true since all managers are deleted, but it relies on knowing that `snmp1` is a valid subscription ID format that the BMC would assign. On a freshly started BMC the ID counter may have advanced past `snmp1` (e.g., `snmp10`, `snmp11`); while the test still gets a 404, the brittle ID makes the test harder to understand and may break on firmware that uses different ID schemes.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  Redfish.Delete  ${subscription_uri}/non_existing_snmp_manager  valid_status_codes\u003d[${HTTP_NOT_FOUND}]\n  ```\n\n**Why**: An explicitly invalid URI removes the ambiguity about ID assignment and makes the test self-documenting. This pattern is also less likely to fail on firmware with different subscription ID naming.",
