      "message": "**Issue #2 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: SSH connection from `Start SNMP Manager` is not closed on test failure\n\n**Issue**: `Start SNMP Manager` opens an SSH connection aliased `snmp_server`. The test explicitly calls `SSHLibrary.Execute Command  sudo killall snmptrapd` (line 316) and reads output (line 315) only in the happy path. If `BMC Execute Command` (line 311) or an assertion before it raises an exception, `snmptrapd` is left running on the remote host and the SSH connection is left open. The suite-level `FFDC On Test Case Fail` teardown does not close this SSH connection.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  Generate Error On BMC When SNMP Manager Is Not Configured\n      [Documentation]  Verify that generating an error log on BMC when no SNMP manager is configured\n      ...              results in no SNMP trap being sent to the listener.\n      [Tags]  Generate_Error_On_BMC_When_SNMP_Manager_Is_Not_Configured\n      [Teardown]  Run Keywords\n      ...  SSHLibrary.Switch Connection  snmp_server  AND\n      ...  SSHLibrary.Execute Command  sudo killall snmptrapd\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Leaving `snmptrapd` running between test cases can cause subsequent tests that start a new listener to receive stale trap packets from a prior BMC error, producing false failures.",
      "revId": "b8d4b9e15184d0c548ff4aa4dc06df314cad0d03",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
