      "message": "**Issue #3 (🟢 Low Severity (NICE TO FIX))**: `Delete All SNMP Managers` keyword lacks `[Documentation]` argument descriptions\n\n**Issue**: The keyword has no arguments, so no argument block is strictly needed. However, the keyword silently does nothing when no SNMP managers are configured (empty list → loop does not execute). This edge case is not documented, which may confuse future maintainers who wonder if a \"no managers configured\" state will cause a failure.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  [Documentation]  Delete all SNMP managers currently configured on BMC.\n  ...              No-op if no managers are configured.\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Explicit documentation of the no-op behavior prevents maintainers from adding unnecessary guard checks.",
